## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | 2 |
| **High** | 0 |
| **Medium** | 2 |
| **Low** | 1 |

This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. All 10 public methods on `ProductCatalog` are called, driving line coverage to ~95%, but **6 of 10 tests have zero assertions** and the remaining 4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull` — a trivially-true check that verifies nothing about correctness. This fully explains "95% coverage, bugs in production."

---

### Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic) — all 10 tests

Every public method is called in declaration order with no meaningful verification. The suite inflates coverage while proving nothing.

| Test Method | Assertion | Verifies Behavior? |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (L17) | ❌ None | No |
| `GetProduct_Works` (L23) | `IsNotNull` | No — doesn't check SKU, Name, or Price |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (L31) | ❌ None | No — never checks the price changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (L38) | ❌ None | No — never checks the product is gone |
| `SearchProducts_Works` (L45) | `IsNotNull` | No — doesn't check result count or contents |
| `GetAllProducts_Works` (L55) | `IsNotNull` | No — doesn't check count or contents |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (L63) | ❌ None | No — discards the return value entirely |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68) | ❌ None | No — never checks prices changed |
| `ExportToCsv_Works` (L77) | `IsNotNull` | No — doesn't check CSV content |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85) | ❌ None | No — never checks product was imported |

**Fix — example for 3 representative tests:**

```csharp
// AddProduct_Works → AddProduct_StoresProductRetrievableBySku
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProductRetrievableBySku()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}

// UpdatePrice_Works → UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}

